  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Connecticut has $16B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal buying community made 22,171 awards in the state so far, with an average award size of $721K, and obligations fell 54.5% year over year. The Department of Defense dominates buying in Connecticut, obligating $15.6B, which accounts for the vast majority of the current-year total. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations at $6.9B, followed by Aircraft Manufacturing at $3.2B and Ship Building and Repairing at $1.7B. Large prime contractors are concentrated in naval and aerospace work: ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION has $8.6B, RTX CORPORATION has $3.7B, and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION has $2.7B. Past fiscal years show large swings in state obligations, including $35.1B in FY25 and $26B in FY23, which frame the current-year decline. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations only. Use these totals to prioritize outreach to the Department of Defense and to suppliers in engineering, aircraft manufacturing, and shipbuilding sectors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies award the most federal contracts in Connecticut?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $15.6B in Connecticut in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $108M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $105M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Justice with $30.5M and the Department of Labor with $17.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal contractors operating in Connecticut?",
        "body": "ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION leads vendors with $8.6B in obligations in FY2026 to date. RTX CORPORATION has $3.7B and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION has $2.7B. Additional top vendors include HAMILTON SUNDSTRAND CORPORATION at $97.9M and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $58.6M."
      }
